Executive Summary
This report presents the results of a Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing (VAPT) conducted on NovaTech’s internal network and systems.
The assessment identified several critical, high and medium-risk vulnerabilities, including exposed database services, weak authentication mechanisms, unauthorised access, outdated Apache webserver, and lack of network segmentation. 
Security monitoring alerts also revealed suspicious activities such as brute-force login attempts, unauthorized FTP access, and abnormal outbound traffic from the web server.
These findings indicate a likelihood of a full system compromise, with potential risks including data breaches, unauthorized access, and lateral movement within the network. Immediate remediation is strongly recommended.
