Security Recommendations
1.	Enable Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) using authenticators.
2.	Restrict Database access by closing unnecessary ports (3306, 21, 445) or configuring firewall rule.
3.	Patch and update all systems by regularly updating security patches. 
4.	Enforce strong password policies by defining lock-out policy, password length and complexity requirements.
5.	Implement network segmentation by separating Webserver, Database and internal systems.
6.	Replace FTP with SFTP by disabling ftp service and configuring ssh for more secure connection.
7.	Deploy monitoring tools (IDS/IPS, SIEM)
